<title>USA: MOSCOM to cut costs, consolidate operations.</title>
<headline>MOSCOM to cut costs, consolidate operations.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSFORD, N.Y. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>MOSCOM Corp said on Tuesday that it will cut its operating expenses by $2 million, or $0.28 a share, annually by reducing its Votan unit's operations in Pleasanton, Calif., and consolidating the remainder of them into MOSCOM's operations in Pittsford, N.Y.</p>
<p>MOSCOM said it will continue to market products using Votan technology, including a voice activated information system.  </p>
<p>The company was not immediately available for further comment about the cost cutting measures.</p>
</text>
